{
  "h1": [
    "One drop of soap,",
    "and floating pepper races",
    "to the edge",
    "of the bowl.",
    "Nothing touched it.",
    "So what pulls the pepper?"
  ],
  "h2": [
    "Not the soap.",
    "Clean water further out pulls",
    "harder than the soapy spot,",
    "and drags the surface outward.",
    "In one lab study,",
    "that surface",
    "reached up to 0.5m/s."
  ],
  "h3": [
    "Yet with soap",
    "fed in steadily,",
    "the rush",
    "stops at a ring.",
    "Why there?"
  ],
  "h4": [
    "Here is the engine.",
    "At 25 degrees,",
    "clean water pulls",
    "harder than our soap, SDS",
    "at an inferred 25 millimolar",
    "in water:",
    "a gap of about",
    "36mN/m, calculated.",
    "That gap,",
    "not the soap itself,",
    "does the pulling."
  ],
  "c1": [
    "Every patch of that surface",
    "pulls on its neighbours.",
    "Over clean water",
    "the pull is strong;",
    "over the soapy spot",
    "it is weaker."
  ],
  "p1": [
    "Over clean water",
    "the pull is strong;",
    "over the soapy spot",
    "it is weaker.",
    "The surface is dragged outward,",
    "and the water just",
    "below is dragged along.",
    "A flow",
    "driven by a difference",
    "in pull like this",
    "is called a Marangoni flow."
  ],
  "p2": [
    "How do you measure",
    "such a flow?",
    "Roché and colleagues",
    "pumped soap solution steadily",
    "through a fine needle",
    "onto centimetre-thick layers",
    "of ultrapure water,",
    "rated 18.2 megohm centimetres.",
    "Olive oil droplets ten micrometres",
    "across were added to scatter",
    "light and trace the motion."
  ],
  "p3": [
    "They tested eight surfactants, bought",
    "ninety nine per cent pure,",
    "with different tails and heads.",
    "Their micelle thresholds",
    "span two orders of magnitude.",
    "One of them is SDS.",
    "Another study measured its",
    "threshold at 25 degrees,",
    "with no salt added:",
    "8.23, in millimolar units."
  ],
  "p4": [
    "Why does",
    "that threshold matter here?",
    "Below it,",
    "extra molecules",
    "crowd onto the surface.",
    "Above it,",
    "they clump into micelles",
    "in the water.",
    "Roché's model takes the threshold,",
    "the critical micelle concentration,",
    "as the soap concentration right",
    "at the needle."
  ],
  "p5": [
    "Now the balance.",
    "The gap in pull,",
    "spread over the size",
    "of the soapy patch,",
    "must be matched",
    "by friction inside a thin",
    "moving layer of water.",
    "In Roché's model,",
    "viscosity times surface speed",
    "over that layer's thickness",
    "roughly equals the gap",
    "over the patch radius."
  ],
  "p6": [
    "Back to the bowl.",
    "Pepper grains float,",
    "so they",
    "ride on the surface.",
    "When the surface slides outward,",
    "the grains go with it.",
    "Roché's paper",
    "opens with this very trick:",
    "the grains,",
    "it says,",
    "are transported rapidly",
    "to the edge",
    "of the bowl."
  ],
  "c2": [
    "Under steady pumping,",
    "Roché saw three zones:",
    "the source at the needle,",
    "a clear zone around it",
    "where tracers are swept away,",
    "and an outer zone",
    "with pairs of swirls."
  ],
  "v1": [
    "Outside the clear zone,",
    "the surface barely moves.",
    "The paper puts it plainly:",
    "further from the source,",
    "the tracers move only slightly.",
    "So the fast flow",
    "is confined.",
    "It fills the clear zone",
    "and no more."
  ],
  "v2": [
    "Inside the clear zone",
    "the surface starts slowly,",
    "around one centimetre per second",
    "near the needle.",
    "It speeds up,",
    "reaching a peak near 0.5m/s,",
    "then slows gradually",
    "as it crosses the rest",
    "of the zone."
  ],
  "v3": [
    "Then comes the surprise.",
    "At the edge",
    "of the clear zone,",
    "the gradual slowdown turns sudden.",
    "The tracers decelerate abruptly,",
    "and the fast surface flow",
    "ends right there.",
    "That edge is",
    "the ring from the start."
  ],
  "v4": [
    "Where does the water go?",
    "It cannot pile up",
    "at the edge.",
    "Below the clear zone,",
    "the paper traces a flow",
    "that follows the bottom",
    "of the container",
    "back towards the source.",
    "Surface out and bottom back",
    "make one loop."
  ],
  "v5": [
    "Pump faster,",
    "and you might",
    "expect a faster flow.",
    "Not here.",
    "For one shorter tailed sulfate,",
    "the paper reports",
    "that the injection flow rate",
    "has little effect",
    "on the velocity field.",
    "What pumping does",
    "change is the size",
    "of the clear zone."
  ],
  "v6": [
    "Tail length matters far more.",
    "Double the number",
    "of carbon atoms",
    "in the tail,",
    "and the radius",
    "of the clear zone changes",
    "over almost two",
    "orders of magnitude.",
    "Longer tails",
    "have lower micelle thresholds",
    "and make bigger zones."
  ],
  "v7": [
    "The head matters too.",
    "Keep a twelve carbon tail",
    "and swap only the head:",
    "the sulfate head of SDS",
    "gives a smaller",
    "clear zone than a trimethylammonium",
    "bromide head.",
    "Same tail,",
    "different head,",
    "different ring."
  ],
  "c3": [
    "Now the open question:",
    "why does the flow stop",
    "at a ring?",
    "Molecules leave the needle.",
    "Each one",
    "rides the surface outward,",
    "but it can also leave",
    "the surface and dissolve",
    "into the water below."
  ],
  "w1": [
    "Roché's model rests",
    "on one assumption:",
    "the flow stops when",
    "the injected surfactants have all",
    "desorbed from the interface.",
    "Past that point the surface",
    "is clean again,",
    "the pull is even,",
    "and nothing drives the flow.",
    "The ring marks where soap",
    "runs out on the surface."
  ],
  "w2": [
    "How fast should",
    "the surface go?",
    "Roché's speed law,",
    "with its",
    "constant set to one,",
    "uses the pull gap,",
    "viscosity, density and patch size.",
    "Take our",
    "gap of about 36mN/m,",
    "water's viscosity at 25 degrees,",
    "and Roché's own patch estimate",
    "of fifteen millimetres:",
    "0.46m/s, calculated."
  ],
  "w3": [
    "That lands close",
    "to the 0.5m/s Roché measured.",
    "The same model",
    "gives the thickness",
    "of the moving layer:",
    "the square root",
    "of kinematic viscosity times",
    "patch size over speed.",
    "That is 0.17 millimetres, calculated.",
    "A sheet",
    "that thin drags the surface",
    "across the dish."
  ],
  "w4": [
    "The soap layer",
    "is thinner still.",
    "Soap molecules spread through",
    "water far more",
    "slowly than motion does.",
    "The paper's ratio,",
    "the Schmidt number,",
    "is roughly ten thousand.",
    "Its square root",
    "sets the gap,",
    "so the soap layer is",
    "a hundred times thinner, calculated."
  ],
  "w5": [
    "Now the ring size.",
    "Roché's second law",
    "says the zone radius",
    "grows with the pumping rate",
    "to the power three quarters,",
    "and shrinks",
    "as the micelle threshold rises.",
    "Double the pumping,",
    "and the ring",
    "grows 1.68 times, calculated.",
    "With a threshold",
    "of ten millimolar,",
    "the paper's estimate",
    "is fifteen millimetres."
  ],
  "w6": [
    "Two more checks.",
    "Make the water layer more",
    "viscous and the zone grows,",
    "as the paper's supplement shows.",
    "And the speed law",
    "fails when the clear zone",
    "is as small",
